# Growth Ladder

## How to place the account

| Phase | Evidence | Typical size |
|---|---|---|
| **0 Foundation** | OAuth not proven or ~0–1 sub | 0–1 sub |
| **1 First converts** | Login works; posting several times/week | 0–20 |
| **2 Repeatable** | Lists + vault in use; some PPV sold | ~10–50 |
| **3 Monetization** | Chat revenue measurable | ~50–200 |
| **4 Traffic** | One channel produces weekly new subs | ~200–1,000 |
| **5 Scale** | Team or real automation | 1,000+ |

Code: `phaseFromSubscriberCount` in `src/lib/ops/phase.ts`. Unauthenticated default: **1 sub / Phase 0**.

## Phase 0 — NOW

OAuth, bio, 7-day manual content plan, welcome templates. Do not auto-post or auto-DM.

## Phase 1 — ONE AHEAD (smallest slice)

One traffic checklist, 3-item PPV menu, 2–3 lists. No ads, no multi-channel spam.

## Phases 2–5

Repeatable chat + catalog, then monetization systems, then traffic engine, then scale. **Do not start here.**

## Realistic 3-month plan (Phase 0 start)

- Month 1: 0–25 subs, $0–$300
- Month 2: 15–60 subs, $100–$1,000
- Month 3: 40–150 subs, $400–$3,000 typical; ~$5k is an outlier

**$1M in 3 months is a hallucination.** $1M/month implies on the order of 20k–50k paying fans at beginner ARPU, or whales this page does not have.

## Promotion is earned

Do not skip phases because the user is excited. Ship the Phase 0 artifact (usually login or this week’s posts) and decline the rest.
